If elongating the finger is your goal, you have already narrowed it down to these two shapes.

The marquise cut is the longest-looking diamond at any given carat weight. Its football silhouette — two pointed tips, a curved body — creates more finger extension per carat than any other shape in existence. The emerald cut is rectangular with a long face-up profile and cropped corners, creating a sleek, architectural elongation that looks very different from the marquise's dramatic sweep.

Both are elongated. Both slim the finger.

They are not interchangeable.

The marquise is a brilliant cut with 58 facets. It sparkles. It also has bow tie risk at both ends — two dark shadows, one at each pointed tip, that must be evaluated on video before buying.

The emerald cut has no bow tie, no pointed tips, and no scattered sparkle. What it has is a hall-of-mirrors depth that no brilliant cut can replicate.

Choosing between them is a choice between dramatic and elegant, lively and calm, maximum visual impact and quiet confidence.

Most buyers who land on this comparison have already eliminated round and oval. They know they want something elongated and distinctive. The marquise gives you the most finger coverage per dollar of any shape.

The emerald gives you the most refined, architectural look of any shape. Understanding what each shape actually demands — in clarity, color, setting, and evaluation process — is what this guide is for.

This guide covers both shapes in full — geometry, The Double Bow Tie risk, pricing from 1ct to 4ct, clarity and color minimums, face-up size comparison, and the exact buyer who should choose each shape.

---

**TL;DR — Which Elongates More?**

**Marquise elongates more.** A 1ct marquise at a 2.00 L:W ratio measures approximately 10.5×5.3mm — the longest face-up profile of any 1ct diamond. A 1ct emerald at 1.40 L:W measures approximately 7.0×5.0mm. At equal carats, the marquise covers more finger length every time.

- Marquise: brilliant cut, 58 facets, sparkles, bow tie risk at BOTH tips, two pointed tips requiring V-prongs, VS2 clarity floor.
- Emerald: step cut, hall-of-mirrors, no bow tie, VS1 minimum, G color minimum in platinum, shorter face-up than marquise.
- Natural emerald 1ct GIA D-VS1 from [$3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural emerald 2ct GIA F-VS1 from [$24,407](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/14013191?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).
- Lab emerald 2ct IGI D-FL from [$4,735](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28828463?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Lab emerald 3ct IGI D-IF from [$9,235](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28885081?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).
- → Choose marquise for maximum finger elongation and brilliant sparkle. → Choose emerald for architectural elegance and the hall-of-mirrors look.

