## Natural Diamond Price Comparison: Marquise vs Emerald Cut

Marquise diamonds are currently undervalued relative to their visual impact. The shape fell out of fashion in the 1990s, and while it has recovered strongly, it still trades at a modest discount to the most popular fancy shapes like oval and pear.

That discount benefits buyers who choose marquise deliberately.

At 1ct, a well-graded marquise in G-VS2 runs approximately $3,500–$5,000 depending on cut quality and specific proportions. A 1ct GIA G-VS2 emerald requires VS1 minimum for eye-clean quality and runs comparable or higher at similar color grades, because the emerald's open table forces buyers to spend up on clarity.

