## Clarity: What Each Shape Hides

The marquise cut's 58 brilliant facets fragment and scatter inclusions across the face of the stone. VS2 is a safe clarity floor for marquise. SI1 can work in the center of the stone, away from the tips, where the facets are most active at hiding inclusions.

The tips of a marquise are a different matter.

Inclusions near the pointed tips of a marquise are more visible than inclusions in the center, because the facets at the very tip are smaller and provide less fragmentation. For marquise diamonds with inclusions near the tips, upgrade to VS2 minimum at the tip location.

The emerald cut's open table shows inclusions clearly across the entire face of the stone. VS1 is the non-negotiable minimum. VS2 can occasionally work if the inclusion is at the far edge of the table or girdle — but this requires reviewing the GIA clarity plot and video before accepting.

